# A CRLF checkout of a shipped hook is not cosmetic: bash reads `then\r` as a
# command, so the hook dies mid-verdict and every tool call it gates is denied
# with a syntax error (probe-verified: exit 2). The data files beside it fail more
# quietly — a trailing CR on a gentle-manifest.txt line makes every
# `[ -e "$CLAUDE_DIR/$rel" ]` test miss, so the legacy cleanup removes nothing and
# all three of its readers agree it succeeded.
#
# ONE rule for the whole tree rather than a list of names or a glob per extension,
# both of which were reopened by whichever file landed next. `text=auto` rather
# than `text`, so a binary added later is decided by its own content.
#
# install.bat, verify.bat and install.ps1 are LF here against the platform
# convention, deliberately: LF is the form that has actually been run, and CRLF
# would ship one nothing here has. Reversing that takes an override line under
# this one and a run behind it.
#
# This pin renormalizes no clone that already exists, so the manifest's three
# readers strip the CR themselves.
* text=auto eol=lf
